  "answer": "This is a manufacturer website field on the private REST API. I'll follow the feature playbook and look at how manufacturers are stored and returned today.The website is an optional string on the manufacturer. Invalid values have to fail in the API method before the existing catch turns every error into 503. I'll put the field on the shared model and copy it through the populators that build manufacturer JSON.Manufacturers now have an optional `website` URL. It is a nullable `WEBSITE` column on the manufacturer entity, accepted on private create and update, and copied into manufacturer JSON for the detail and list endpoints and for the manufacturer nested in a product. A value that does not start with `http://` or `https://` is rejected with HTTP 400 before anything is saved. Per Model the Domain, the field lives on the existing manufacturer types instead of a separate object. Maven compile of the affected modules succeeded. The REST flow was not exercised.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core-model,sm-shop-model,sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": \"HTTP 400 on a bad website, persistence of a valid website, and the website field in manufacturer detail, list, and product JSON\", \"missing\": \"a focused manufacturer API test or a documented way to boot the private REST API against the test database\"}",
